% Approved cross-component contract: build_notes.py, ../Studies, ../documents/notes.
% Scope is the three worked examples and their document/evidence tooling only.
% Direct implementation; no completed PDD generation/sync is claimed.

Build a shared-source thematic LaTeX master and Numerical Recipes/Wie/Sutton
companions in portrait and 1200x700pt two-column screen editions. Run LaTeX
without shell escape, resolve bibliographies and cross-references, and reject
overfull boxes. Keep all intermediates and published results outside tracked
source. Record source/output hashes and build time; publish only after all
eight documents compile successfully.

Each study states mathematical spaces, assumptions, frames, units, chosen
synthetic data and evidence limits. Numerical implementations are independent
of proprietary textbook distributions. Sage is the primary symbolic system.
Use only an installed prebuilt Docker image, with no pull/build and no network
for batch checks; record immutable image ID and actual runtime versions.

Oscillator: derive velocity Verlet and its modified invariant; exact symplectic
and invariant checks; analytic finite-time convergence and bounded energy test.
Rigid body: derive Euler equations for body spin and body-to-inertial R;
symbolically verify energy/momentum-norm derivatives; compare axisymmetric
solution and test energy, inertial momentum, R^TR and determinant numerically.
Nozzle: derive area–Mach relation with perfect-gas/isentrope assumptions;
check sonic/Mach-2 cases and derivative in Sage, solve both physical branches,
and verify mass flux independently. Reject invalid domains and branch names.

MUST NOT equate finite numerical tests with general mathematical proof,
physical validation, exact SO(3) preservation by RK4, or verification of linked
legacy code. Reports include inputs, thresholds, measured metrics, timestamps,
versions and hashes; failed runs preserve prior evidence and changed inputs
make old evidence stale.
